Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "NighttimeUrbanTrafficWithPoliceActivity" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :EvidenceBasedAnomaly ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1, :obstacle2 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3, :risk4 .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Police vehicle with emergency lights active" .

:obstacle2 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Yellow taxi vehicle in adjacent lane" .

:weather1 a :NightCondition .

:risk1 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Potential occlusion due to police vehicle lights and activity" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential rear-end collision risk due to police vehicle presence" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :LaneIntrusionRisk ;
    :description "Taxi vehicle in adjacent lane may intrude into current lane" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:risk4 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Wet road conditions may affect vehicle handling" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev4 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.80"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.65"^^xsd:float .

:sev4 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.55"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

